[$in title:["Structs and methods"]]
[$in description:["Declare structs, construct values and call shared or mutable receiver methods in Moth."]]
[$in head:[language_theme_head]]

[navbar]
[sidebar]
listed = sync_navigation(sidebar_id)!
[section, $md:
    # Structs and methods

    A struct gives a name to a type and its fields. Use its constructor to
    supply the field values. Define a method in the same file when you want
    to give values of that type an operation of their own.

    @#receiver-methods (Receiver methods) shows how to read a value through
    a method. @#mutable-receivers (Mutable receivers) shows how to change it.
]

